Match Wine MCIAVI microsecond clock conversion and frame deadlines.

Wine currenttime_us performs QPC integer multiply/divide before converting
its microseconds to double. MCIAVI_player snapshots that clock and adds each
PaintFrame duration to the next deadline. Separately flooring the movie epoch
and each reading to milliseconds can make native/WASM frames due almost
one millisecond early. Use the microsecond provider and the original double
next-deadline accumulation. Native mirrors Wine QPC's signed x86 arithmetic;
browser retains its independently observed output-time source at microsecond
resolution. Keep the legacy millisecond provider for audio drain polls.

This changes neither decoded pixels nor submitted source PCM. Actual browser
clock synchronization, original/port scheduling and full audio tails remain
separate acceptance requirements.

Primary sources:
https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/wine-10.0/dlls/mciavi32/mciavi.c
https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/wine-10.0/dlls/mciavi32/mmoutput.c

